  "query_preview": "..\nAn unsettled weather pattern produced by an extensive monsoon trough\ndominated primarily by a developing disturbance known as Invest 93W \nwell to the east, is expected to continue as such the next few days.\nMostly dry conditions are expected overnight, followed by some\nisland showers developing Tuesday afternoon. After, conditions will\ndeteriorate once again as Invest 93W continues to consolidate and\npass to the northeast of the Marianas sometime Thursday through \nFriday, inducing a significant monsoon surge that will bring a peak \nin shower and thunder potential by the weekend. Conditions are then \nexpected to remain wet coming into next week as a southerwesterly \nmonsoon regime continues.",
